  "executive_summary": "This paper establishes that the systems of Hecke eigenvalues appearing in the coherent cohomology of any mod p abelian type compact Shimura variety at hyperspecial level are identical to those appearing in any Hecke-equivariant closed subscheme. The author generalizes previous results by Goldring-Koskivirta and Terakado-Yu, which were limited to smooth, zero-dimensional subschemes, to include higher-dimensional and possibly singular subschemes. The central result, Theorem A, proves that for a compact abelian type Shimura variety $S_K$ and any prime-to-p Hecke-equivariant closed subscheme $Y_K$, the systems of Hecke eigenvalues in the direct sum of cohomology groups $H^0(S_K, V(\\eta))$ and $H^0(Y_K, V(\\eta))$ are the same. The proof overcomes two main technical obstacles: the absence of nowhere vanishing Hecke-invariant sections on singular subschemes and the failure of the conormal sequence to be exact or consist of locally free sheaves. The author introduces a \"going-down\" argument that intersects the subscheme with the smallest length stratum it meets and successively removes nonsingular points to obtain a smooth, closed subscheme $Z_K$ admitting a nowhere vanishing Hecke-equivariant section. By relating eigenvalues on $Y_K$ and $S_K$ to those on $Z_K$, the author proves the equivalence. The paper also extends these results to noncompact Shimura varieties and nonclosed subschemes, such as Ekedahl-Oort strata, length strata, and central leaves, under specific conditions regarding properness and closure. These findings unify the spectral properties of Hecke actions across various geometric strata of Shimura varieties, providing a robust framework for understanding the arithmetic geometry of these spaces.",
